\label{lem:a}
Let $(b_i)_{i\geq 1}$ be a sequence of positive reals with $b_i\rightarrow\infty$.  Given $s\in \mathbb{N}$ and $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $t>s$ and a non-increasing sequence $a_{s+1},\dots ,a_t$ of positive reals, such that
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] $\sum_{i=s+1}^t a_i b_i\geq 1$,
\item[(ii)] $a_ib_i\le \varepsilon$ for all $i$, and
\item[(iii)] $\sum_{i=s+1}^t a_i\leq \varepsilon$.
\end{enumerate}
